          ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{2} &=5{x}_{1}-12 \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{1}}{3} &=2-3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=-12 \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{1}}{3}+3{x}_{2} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 5 & -12 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"
